9. Requests the Secretary-General to report to the Security Council on the implementation of the BINUH mandate every 90 days, including on progress against clear benchmarks related to political stability, security, rule of law, human rights, sexual and gender-based violence, grave violations against children, humanitarian access, climate-related security risks, and implementation of the arms embargo and sanctions regime, including with sex- and age-disaggregated data, with the first report by 15 October 2025 and a final report by 15 June 2026;

10. Affirms that it shall keep the situation in Haiti under continuous review and expresses its intention to review the BINUH mandate by 15 January 2026, or earlier if necessary, on the basis of the reports of the Secretary-General and developments on the ground;

